  "phoneSafeShadeTitle": "Lock the notification shade on the lock screen",
  "phoneSafeShadeWhy": "Stops a thief from turning off data or airplane mode before you can locate the phone.",
  "phoneSafeShadeHowStock": "Open Settings > Display & lock screen (or Lock screen).\nFind 'Show notifications on lock screen' or 'Quick settings on lock screen'.\nTurn off access to quick settings / the control panel while locked.",
  "phoneSafeShadeHowRealme": "Open Settings > Notification & status bar.\nTurn off 'Pull down status bar when locked' or 'Control Center on lock screen'.\nAlso turn off 'Toggle Airplane/Mobile data from locked shade'.",
  "phoneSafeShadeHowSamsung": "Open Settings > Lock screen > Secure lock settings.\nTurn off 'Show quick panel on lock screen' / notification panel access.\nRe-enter your PIN to save.",
  "phoneSafeShadeHowXiaomi": "Open Settings > Lock screen (or Always-on & Lock screen).\nTurn off 'Control Center on lock screen' / 'Notification shade when locked'.\nUnder Security, turn off toggling connectivity from the locked shade.",
  "phoneSafeShadeHowVivo": "Open Settings > Status bar & notification.\nTurn off 'Pull down Control Center when locked'.\nUnder Lock screen, block quick toggles while locked.",
  "phoneSafePowerOffTitle": "Require PIN to power off",
  "phoneSafePowerOffWhy": "A thief can't switch the phone off (so you can't track it) without your PIN.",
  "phoneSafePowerOffHowGeneric": "Open Settings and search 'power off' or 'verification'.\nIf your phone supports it, turn on 'Verify identity to power off' / 'Lock before power off'.\nIf you don't find it, your phone may not support this yet.",
  "phoneSafePowerOffHowRealme": "Open Settings > Password & security > System security.\nTurn on 'Require password to power off' (if present on your ColorOS version).\nConfirm with your PIN.",
  "phoneSafePowerOffHowXiaomi": "Open Settings > Passwords & security > Privacy.\nLook for 'Lock after power off' / 'Verify to shut down'.\nTurn it on and confirm with your PIN.",
  "phoneSafeTheftTitle": "Turn on Google Theft Protection",
  "phoneSafeTheftWhy": "Auto-locks the phone if it's snatched, kept offline, or someone tries a reset.",
  "phoneSafeTheftHow": "Open Settings > Google > All services > Theft Protection (or search 'Theft Protection').\nTurn on 'Theft Detection Lock'.\nTurn on 'Offline Device Lock'.\nTurn on 'Remote Lock' and verify your phone number.",
  "phoneSafeFindTitle": "Enable Find My Device / Find Hub",
  "phoneSafeFindWhy": "Lets you locate, ring, lock, or erase the phone remotely — even when it's offline.",
  "phoneSafeFindHow": "Open Settings > Google > Find My Device (or Find Hub) and turn it on.\nChoose 'Find your offline devices' > 'With network in all areas'.\nMake sure Location is on for the phone.\nTest it by signing in at google.com/android/find.",
  "phoneSafeFindOpenWeb": "Open Find My Device (web)",
  "phoneSafeSimTitle": "Lock your SIM with a PIN",
  "phoneSafeSimWhy": "Stops a thief from moving your number to another phone to bypass OTP security.",
  "phoneSafeSimHow": "Open Settings > Security > SIM lock (or Settings > SIM card).\nTurn on 'Lock SIM card'.\nSet a SIM PIN (ask your operator for the default if unsure, then change it).\nNote: too many wrong tries can block the SIM — keep the PUK safe.",
  "phoneSafeLockTitle": "Use a strong screen lock",
  "phoneSafeLockWhy": "A 6+ digit PIN or password is far harder to guess or shoulder-surf than a pattern.",
  "phoneSafeLockHow": "Open Settings > Security > Screen lock.\nChoose PIN (6+ digits) or a password — avoid pattern.\nTurn off 'Make pattern visible' if you keep a pattern anywhere.\nAdd fingerprint/face only as a convenience, not as your only lock.",
  "phoneSafeFrpTitle": "Add a Google account (Factory Reset Protection)",
  "phoneSafeFrpWhy": "With a Google account signed in, a thief can't reuse the phone after a reset without your login.",
  "phoneSafeFrpHow": "Open Settings > Accounts and make sure a Google account is signed in.\nRemember this account's email and password — FRP will ask for it after a reset.\nDon't remove the account before selling or giving the phone away (reset it properly instead).",
